# Kundalini Spines — static site, no build step, no dependencies.
# Almost everything here is source and belongs in the repo, including the
# assets: the site cannot deploy without them and they total ~88 MB, well
# inside GitHub's limits (100 MB per file, 1 GB soft repo limit).

# ---- Backups and masters (never commit) ----
# The 885 MB Kundalini-Spines-Track-Art masters folder lives outside this
# directory and must stay out. The backup zips are snapshots of this repo —
# committing them would double the repo on every snapshot.
ks-backup-*.zip
*-Track-Art*.zip
_to_delete/

# ---- OS / editor noise ----
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# ---- One-time setup scaffolding ----
# setup/ exists only to create this repo (see setup/README-SETUP.md). Its job is
# done after the first commit; it is not part of the site.
setup/

# ---- Local server / tooling ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.env
.env.*

# ---- Deliberately NOT ignored, so nobody "tidies" them away later ----
# js/music-page.js and js/audio-player.js are loaded by no page. They are the
# reference implementation for a future all-tracks directory page and are kept
# on purpose — see docs/06-legacy-music-page.md.
# raster-test.html and raster-test-2.html are the sharpness harness.
# transmissions-options.html and transmissions-option5-v2.html are design
# mockups, noindex and unlinked. All are tracked intentionally.
